 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Extension of a rational map to a proper target (Conrad)",
 "statement": "Let $S$ be qcqs, let $X$ be a qcqs $S$-scheme, let $U\\subseteq X$ be a dense\nquasi-compact open subscheme, and let $Y\\to S$ be proper and of finite type.\nEvery $S$-morphism $f\\colon U\\to Y$ extends to an $S$-morphism\n$\\widetilde f\\colon\\widetilde X\\to Y$ on some $U$-admissible blow-up\n$\\widetilde X\\to X$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-cor-nagata-sketch-proper-extension/cor-nagata-conrad-proper-target-extension.md",
  "place": "node cor-nagata-conrad-proper-target-extension, order 225"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-nagata-admissible-blowup",
  "def-nagata-global-blowup"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Take $V=U$. By\n[lemma-nagata-conrad-morphism-is-quasi-domination], $(U,f)$ is a\nquasi-domination of $U$ over $Y$, because a proper morphism is separated.\n[thm-nagata-conrad-elimination] gives a $U$-admissible blow-up\n$\\widetilde X\\to X$ and a quasi-domination $(W,\\widetilde f)$ of\n$\\widetilde X$ over $Y$ extending $f$. Since $Y\\to S$ is proper,\n[lemma-nagata-conrad-quasi-domination-proper-target] forces $W$ to be\nall of $\\widetilde X$.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-conrad-morphism-is-quasi-domination",
    "thm-nagata-conrad-elimination",
    "lemma-nagata-conrad-quasi-domination-proper-target"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
